Chapter: BuiltinNarrowProven

 Second slice of the bounds-prover reach campaign
 (BoundsProverReach.md): a builtin whose return is structurally
 bounded proves at a bounded store. `list-length` cannot exceed
 2^32 - 1 in a 4 GB address space, so storing it into a field bounded
 0..4294967295 is proven (CDX2053). The same value into a 0..255
 field is not provable and is rejected since CDX2051 became an
 error; that twin lives in errors/narrowing-unproven. The sidecars
 pin the proven diagnostic and the in-range runtime behavior.

Section: Definitions

  Meta = record {
   count : Integer between 0 and 4294967295
  }

  measure : List Integer -> Meta
  measure (xs) = Meta { count = list-length xs }

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni (integer-to-text ((measure [10, 20, 30]).count))
  end
